      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "1.1",
          "cutStart": 1.8,
          "cutEnd": 4.02,
          "text": "Hey, I'm Taylor. I'm a real human."
        },
        {
          "id": "1.2",
          "cutStart": 4.02,
          "cutEnd": 8.9,
          "text": "I'm also a user experience and product designer, and I'd like to show you something I've been working on."
        },
        {
          "id": "1.3",
          "cutStart": 8.9,
          "cutEnd": 11.1,
          "text": "It's called Color Taylor."
        },
        {
          "id": "2.1",
          "cutStart": 17.46,
          "cutEnd": 25.56,
          "text": "I've always struggled with mixing colors using RGB. It turned out hue and saturation models were helpful for finding the colors that I want."
        },
        {
          "id": "2.2",
          "cutStart": 26.06,
          "cutEnd": 35.16,
          "text": "Let's say I have this turquoise color, but I want to get to teal, which is darker and more colorful. How do I dial that into the RGB?"
        },
        {
          "id": "2.3",
          "cutStart": 35.16,
          "cutEnd": 37.7,
          "text": "I think I need to lower red and blue,"
        },
        {
          "id": "2.4",
          "cutStart": 37.7,
          "cutEnd": 42.58,
          "text": "but how much do I change the RGB before the color becomes unfamiliar?"
        },
        {
          "id": "2.5",
          "cutStart": 54.12,
          "cutEnd": 68.2,
          "text": "Once I understood how hue models and RGB work together, I could more confidently understand how colors were constructed. That made it easier to choose harmonious colors, which I could then build into larger systems."
        },
        {
          "id": "2.6",
          "cutStart": 68.94,
          "cutEnd": 73.16,
          "text": "Our focus for this presentation will be hue, saturation, and brightness."
        },
        {
          "id": "2.7",
          "cutStart": 73.16,
          "cutEnd": 80.06,
          "text": "But the app supports HSL as well, so you can use what's familiar to you."
        },
        {
          "id": "2.8",
          "cutStart": 80.62,
          "cutEnd": 87.06,
          "text": "Color Taylor is meant to be a playground and educational tool for how RGB and HSB work together."
        },
        {
          "id": "2.9",
          "cutStart": 87.56,
          "cutEnd": 93.3,
          "text": "You see the relationships in real time, to help better understand how colors work on your display."
        },
        {
          "id": "2.10",
          "cutStart": 94.78,
          "cutEnd": 97.94,
          "text": "I'll just move myself out of the way, for now."
        },
        {
          "id": "11.1",
          "cutStart": 357.58,
          "cutEnd": 363.22,
          "text": "If you use Figma, I've also made a Color Taylor plugin that you might like to check out."
        },
        {
          "id": "11.2",
          "cutStart": 365.44,
          "cutEnd": 366.7,
          "text": "That's Color Taylor!"
        },
        {
          "id": "11.3",
          "cutStart": 366.7,
          "cutEnd": 378.31,
          "text": "Go play with it, and I hope it helps you see the relationship between RGB and HSB in a different light."
        },
        {
          "id": "11.4",
          "cutStart": 380.53,
          "cutEnd": 385.31,
          "text": "If it's useful, I'd like to hear from you. Questions and feedback are welcome."
        },
        {
          "id": "11.5",
          "cutStart": 385.81,
          "cutEnd": 388.31,
          "text": "Thanks, see ya."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
